From: Fransis <arcadematicas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: adreno a8xx: force GX GDSC collapse before CX in recovery

On SM8750 (Adreno 830) the GX GDSC lives in the separate gxclkctl domain and
feeds the shader cores + the CX GDSC power dependency. After a GMU hang the
firmware leaves GX voted on in HW (RPMH), so CX cannot collapse while GX is up.
The recovery deadlocks ("cx gdsc didn't collapse") and the next hw_init times
out on "GMU OOB GPU_SET" -- which on gamescope/turnip surfaces as VkDeviceLost
(VkResult -4) in the compositor.

ROCKNIX's 0050 (gdsc_gx_disable under synced_poweroff) knows how to collapse GX
but only acts when synced_poweroff is set; this is the caller that sets it in
a8xx_recover(), before the existing CX collapse. Both are needed together.

Tested on the AYN Odin 3 (pocknix-os): the gamescope compositor no longer loses
the device (VkDeviceLost count 0).

Signed-off-by: Fransis <arcadematicas@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a8xx_gpu.c
@@ -904,6 +904,22 @@
 	 */
 	gpu->active_submits = 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * A8xx (SM8750/Adreno 830): the GX GDSC lives in the separate gxclkctl
+	 * domain and feeds the shader cores + the CX GDSC power dependency. On a
+	 * GMU hang the firmware leaves GX voted on in HW (RPMH), so CX cannot
+	 * collapse while GX is up: recovery deadlocks ("cx gdsc didn't
+	 * collapse") and the next hw_init times out on GMU OOB GPU_SET, which
+	 * userspace sees as VkDeviceLost. Force GX collapse BEFORE CX, mirroring
+	 * a6xx_gmu_gxpd_put() (unconditional: gx_is_on() reads false while the
+	 * GMU is hung).
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(gmu->gxpd)) {
+		pm_runtime_get_sync(gmu->gxpd);
+		dev_pm_genpd_synced_poweroff(gmu->gxpd);
+		pm_runtime_put_sync(gmu->gxpd);
+	}
+
 	reinit_completion(&gmu->pd_gate);
 	dev_pm_genpd_add_notifier(gmu->cxpd, &gmu->pd_nb);
 	dev_pm_genpd_synced_poweroff(gmu->cxpd);
-- 
